---
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = `Editorial standards and sourcing | ${site.name}`;
const description =
  "How Everyday Tech Insight selects topics, verifies claims, compares software, separates commercial interests, uses AI assistance, and handles corrections.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/editorial-standards/"
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <Breadcrumbs
      items={[
        { name: "Home", href: "/" },
        {
          name: "Editorial standards",
          href: "/editorial-standards/",
        },
      ]}
    />
    <article class="trust-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">How publication decisions are made</p>
      <h1>Editorial standards</h1>
      <p class="page-deck">
        Every published guide must connect a real business problem to a
        practical technology decision and stay within the evidence available.
      </p>
      <h2>Business technology fit</h2>
      <p>
        A publishable entry identifies the business problem, technology focus,
        intended small-business reader, practical reader outcome, and traceable
        source list. Missing any one of those elements keeps an entry out of the
        public collection.
      </p>
      <h2>Sources and verification</h2>
      <p>
        Current official or primary sources are preferred for technical,
        regulatory, security, and platform claims. Analysis and decision tools
        are described as editorial synthesis when a source does not prescribe
        the exact method. Access dates show when listed sources were checked,
        and material current claims are rechecked before publication.
      </p>
      <h2>Software comparisons and testing</h2>
      <p>
        Software comparisons use stated criteria tied to the business problem,
        such as implementation effort, training, integrations, data export,
        security, privacy, accessibility, support, total cost, and migration
        difficulty. Vendor material may establish documented capabilities, but
        it does not decide the editorial conclusion. Affiliate commission is
        never a comparison criterion.
      </p>
      <p>
        The publication does not describe a product as personally tested, assign
        an unsupported rating, or claim observed results unless a reproducible
        test actually occurred and its limits are documented. The initial public
        portfolio is source-checked, not represented as first-hand product
        testing.
      </p>
      <h2>Dates, updates, and corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Publication and review dates reflect real editorial events, not an
        attempt to manufacture age or freshness. A modification date is used
        only for a substantive change; minor cleanup is not presented as a major
        update. Material corrections are handled under the <a
          href="/corrections/">corrections process</a
        >.
      </p>
      <h2>Independence and commercial relationships</h2>
      <p>
        Advertising and affiliate links are currently inactive. Any future
        sponsorship or material conflict relevant to a guide must be disclosed
        clearly. Advertising, sponsorship, or affiliate relationships do not
        purchase favorable conclusions. Commercial arrangements remain separate
        from topic selection, sourcing, comparison criteria, and corrections.
        Current details appear in the <a href="/advertising-disclosure/"
          >advertising and affiliate disclosure</a
        >.
      </p>
      <h2>AI-assisted workflow and responsibility</h2>
      <p>
        AI tools assisted this initial project with research organization,
        outlining, drafting, editing, and code generation. Sources, citations,
        claims, and generated code remain subject to verification; AI output is
        not treated as evidence merely because it was generated.
      </p>
      <p>
        That assistance does not mean every statement has received human or
        expert review, every product was personally tested, or an unnamed
        specialist approved the work. The owner remains responsible for final
        editorial, privacy, legal, accessibility, and publication review before
        a future AdSense application.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
